# Workflow signals from `devkit workflow next`

Read this when the output of `devkit workflow next --unit <dir>` has a line other than `[WORKFLOW]`, `[DONE]`, `[STAGE]`, `[UNMET]`, `[CHECK]`, `[NEXT_SKILL]` and `[RETURNS]`, or an advisory; read [Stage ids](#stage-ids) for what `next` does not evaluate.

| Line or advisory | Meaning | What to recommend |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `[DELEGATE: role=<role> isolation=...]` | The stage names a support role | Name the role and `spec-delegate`. It is an instruction to follow, not a guarantee the host enforces. |
| `[GATE_PASSED: <gate> stage=<id> policy=auto source=policy]` (JSON `passed_gates`) | The project policy passed this gate; an `auto` gate shows here, not as `[GATE]` | Report the policy delegation as the authority, never as a human approval ([policy](../../spec/references/completion.md#policy)). A choice outside the requested scope still goes to the user. |
| `[WAITING: human gate:<gate>]` with `[REQUEST: id=gate:<gate> ...]` | An `ask` gate decides the next step; the main approval boundaries are `plan-accept`, `proposal-handoff` and `dev-integration`, while `plan-intent` records task intent | Reuse explicit authorization that covers this exact decision; otherwise present it once. Existing user task instructions can satisfy `plan-intent` without another prompt. Record actual authority: a `plan-intent` acceptance with `devkit workflow answer --unit <dir> --request gate:plan-intent --action accept --by user`, a `plan-accept` acceptance only with `devkit spec proposal accept <slug> --by user`, and a decline of either with `devkit workflow answer --unit <dir> --request gate:<gate> --action decline --by user --note "<reason>"` (the decision, never the user's wording). `proposal-handoff` follows the native handoff request; it may share one request with `plan-accept`, while each policy remains independent. `dev-integration` is the next row. Never record or assert an inferred answer. |
{% if execution.environment == "local" %}| `[WAITING: human gate:dev-integration]` (its `[REQUEST]` ends with `answer=given`) | `dev-integration` under `[GATE_POLICY: dev-integration policy=ask]` | Present the verified report and recommend `integration_integrate` for its one native approval (CLI and PR paths: [policy](../../spec/references/completion.md#policy)). The OK is never recorded: re-run `next --given dev-integration`, which then names `integrate`, and pass it on every later run. An objection takes `[RETURNS]` with `devkit workflow return`. |
{% else %}| `[WAITING: human gate:dev-integration]` (its `[REQUEST]` ends with `answer=given`) | `dev-integration` under `[GATE_POLICY: dev-integration policy=ask]` | Present the verified report and return it to the Host unless a separately authorized CLI/PR route exists ([policy](../../spec/references/completion.md#policy)). The OK is never recorded: re-run `next --given dev-integration`, which then names `integrate`, and pass it on every later run. An objection takes `[RETURNS]` with `devkit workflow return`. |
{% endif %}| `[WAITING: runner ...]` | Runner checks (`lint-ci-clean`, `merged`) are confirmed outside this session and show from the start of the stage | Still do the stage's `[NEXT_SKILL]` work (for example `spec-integrate`). Once the runner (CI, the PR merge, or the local cumulative check when no runner exists) has reported, re-run `next` with `--given <check>`. |
| `[PENDING_QUESTION: <file> id=<q> ...]` with `[REQUEST: id=question:worker-NN.<q> ... answer=envelope]` | A run asked the user and waits; the gates from that run's stage on and the handoff are held until all its questions are answered | Present the questions in one round with their options and recommendation. The run that processes the answers records them as an `answer` envelope (the `spec` skill's `references/worker-records.md`), never with `devkit workflow answer`, which refuses them. |
| `[BLOCKED: <file> cause="..." recovery="..."]` (or `malformed=yes reason=...`), `[GATE: ... held=yes]`, unmet `envelope-hold` | The unit is blocked by an unresolved problem or a malformed `worker` envelope (the `spec` skill's `references/worker-records.md` §3) | Show the cause and recommend the recovery (yours inside the approved scope, the user's when the scope must change). Whoever fixes it records a `resolution` naming the file; a malformed envelope is fixed in place (one without a readable stage holds every gate, so `next` may name an earlier stage until then). |
| `[STAGE: collect-feedback ...]` or `[STAGE: direction-handoff ...]` with unmet `frontmatter(proposal.md status reviewing\|accepted)` and detail `status=rejected` | The proposal was rejected: its Planning has ended and no `plan-accept` is asked | Never start a new sweep for it. Report it as ended, waiting for the hygiene cleanup (rejection ADR, then deletion; `SPEC_PROPOSAL_REJECTED_PENDING` in `devkit rules check -p hygiene`). Never set the status back to `reviewing` or record `plan-accept`; reopening the idea is a new draft proposal with a new slug. `status=draft` only means Planning has not started (Backlog may still accept an eligible draft directly). |
| `[DECLINED: id=... note=...]` | The user declined the request; it stays open | Take the work back along the stage's `[RETURNS]` with the note (`devkit workflow return --unit <dir> --to <stage>` for an earlier stage). |
| `[STALE_APPROVAL: ... counts=yes void_with="..."]` | An earlier stage is current while a later stage's approval exists; it still counts | Ask the user whether the redone work needs fresh approval; if so, run the `void_with` command. |
| `[SKIPPED: <id> reason=...]` | The project policy takes this stage out | Report it as skipped, never as done or pending, and do not recommend its skill. |
| `[ENVELOPE_ERROR: <file> "..."]`, `[DECISION_ERROR: <file> "..."]` | A malformed envelope or decision record is ignored (a malformed approval does not count) | A defect to fix before anything else (`devkit workflow envelope check --unit <dir>` for an envelope). |
| `[LINT_ERROR: "..."]` | `lint-clean` could not run; the rules error follows on stderr | Fix what stops `devkit rules check` from running first. |
| `WORKFLOW_NOT_FOUND`, `WORKFLOW_NOT_SELECTED` advisories | The bound workflow has no definition, or the unit is unbound | Follow the advisory's `[FIX]` (`devkit sync`, or `devkit workflow bind --unit <dir> --workflow <id>`). |

`next` reads the anchor's status and binding, `tasks.md`, `reconcile.md`, `envelopes/*.yaml`, `decisions/*.yaml` and the rules. It does not see Git state, PR state, feedback or other units; Steps 1-4 of the skill cover those.

## Stage ids

`sdd-session-feature` and `sdd-session-bugfix` have no unit and are not evaluated by `next`; read them with `devkit workflow show <id>` and diagnose from Steps 1-3. In `sdd-proposal`, `[STAGE: - complete=true]` is the Proposal Hand-off row, and `collect-feedback` is Planning's sweep before `direction-handoff`: [run coverage](../../spec-feedback/references/sweep.md#planning-run-coverage).

